```

### Table: sessions
```sql
id            UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
project_id    UUID REFERENCES projects(id)
client_id     UUID REFERENCES users(id)
status        VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'active'  -- 'active', 'completed', 'abandoned'
started_at    TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
ended_at      TIMESTAMP
total_messages INTEGER DEFAULT 0
drift_events   INTEGER DEFAULT 0
contradiction_events INTEGER DEFAULT 0
stability_score FLOAT DEFAULT 100.0
```

### Table: messages
```sql
id            UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
session_id    UUID REFERENCES sessions(id)
sender        VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL  -- 'client', 'aria', 'system'
content       TEXT NOT NULL         -- enforce max 4000 chars at the schema layer
message_type  VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'normal'  -- 'normal', 'question', 'conflict_alert', 'clarification', 'summary'
created_at    TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
```
*(Messages are append-only. No soft delete, no editing — the conversation
log is the source of truth for the SRS and must not be mutable.)*

### Table: requirement_atoms
```sql
id                UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
session_id        UUID REFERENCES sessions(id)
project_id        UUID REFERENCES projects(id)
subject           VARCHAR(255)
action            VARCHAR(255)
constraint_text    TEXT
raw_text          TEXT NOT NULL   -- enforce max 5000 chars
embedding_id      VARCHAR(255)     -- ChromaDB document ID
embedding_model   VARCHAR(100)     -- e.g. 'all-MiniLM-L6-v2'
embedding_version VARCHAR(30)      -- e.g. 'v1'
status            VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'active'  -- 'active', 'superseded', 'conflicted', 'resolved'
turn_number       INTEGER
created_at        TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
```

### Table: contradictions
```sql
id            UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()
session_id    UUID REFERENCES sessions(id)
atom_1_id     UUID REFERENCES requirement_atoms(id)
atom_2_id     UUID REFERENCES requirement_atoms(id)
similarity_score FLOAT
confidence    FLOAT              -- model's confidence this is a real contradiction, 0.0–1.0
conflict_type VARCHAR(100)       -- 'scope_creep', 'user_shift', 'priority_flip', 'direct_contradiction'
aria_message  TEXT
client_clarification TEXT
resolution    TEXT
resolved_by   UUID REFERENCES users(id)   -- nullable; set when a developer overrides
status        VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'pending'  -- 'pending', 'resolved', 'unresolved', 'ignored'
detected_at   TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
resolved_at   TIMESTAMP
```
*(Models 2-way conflicts only. If you later need 3+ atom conflicts,
introduce a `contradiction_atoms` join table instead of adding `atom_3_id`.)*

